{"info": {"author": null, "author_email": "LiveKit <hello@livekit.io>", "bugtrack_url": null, "classifiers": ["Intended Audience :: Developers", "License :: OSI Approved :: Apache Software License", "Programming Language :: Python :: 3", "Programming Language :: Python :: 3 :: Only", "Programming Language :: Python :: 3.10", "Topic :: Multimedia :: Sound/Audio", "Topic :: Multimedia :: Video", "Topic :: Scientific/Engineering :: Artificial Intelligence"], "description": "# AssemblyAI plugin for LiveKit Agents\n\nSupport for Streaming Speech-to-Text and Streaming Text-to-Speech from AssemblyAI.\n\nMore information is available in the docs for the [STT](https://docs.livekit.io/agents/integrations/stt/assemblyai/) integration and for AssemblyAI's [Streaming TTS](https://www.assemblyai.com/docs/tts/getting-started/quickstart).\n\n## Installation\n\n```bash\npip install livekit-plugins-assemblyai\n```\n\n## Pre-requisites\n\nYou'll need to specify an AssemblyAI API Key. It can be set as environment variable: `ASSEMBLYAI_API_KEY`.\n\n## Usage\n\n```python\nfrom livekit.agents import AgentSession, TurnHandlingOptions\nfrom livekit.plugins import assemblyai\n\nsession = AgentSession(\n    stt=assemblyai.STT(model=\"universal-3-6-pro\", mode=\"balanced\"),\n    tts=assemblyai.TTS(\n        model=\"assemblyai-tts-1\",\n        voice=\"49c443a4-8a1d-5f7e-b70b-98bdbd9823c3\",  # Audrey\n    ),\n    # let AssemblyAI decide when the user has finished speaking\n    turn_handling=TurnHandlingOptions(turn_detection=\"stt\"),\n    # use the TTS word timings for the transcript and for what an interrupted reply said\n    use_tts_aligned_transcript=True,\n    # ... llm, vad, etc.\n)\n```\n\n### Speech-to-text\n\n`assemblyai.STT` streams Universal-3.6 Pro by default (`model`). Useful options:\n\n- `mode`: `\"min_latency\"`, `\"balanced\"` or `\"max_accuracy\"`.\n- `language_codes`: steer transcription toward one or more expected languages (`\"es\"` or\n  `[\"en\", \"es\"]`).\n- `prompt`: context about the audio, such as its domain or scenario, to help recognize likely\n  vocabulary (up to 1,750 characters).\n- `keyterms_prompt`: names and terms the model should get right.\n\n### Text-to-speech\n\n`assemblyai.TTS` streams speech over a pooled WebSocket and cancels in-flight audio when the user\ninterrupts. Useful options:\n\n- `voice`: a voice's id, from the [voice library](https://www.assemblyai.com/docs/tts/voices)\n  or a custom (cloned) voice; defaults to Audrey. Slugs such as `\"aai-linda-3\"` also work, but\n  can change, while ids don't.\n- `language`: a code such as `\"es\"`, set independently of the voice.\n- `model`: defaults to `assemblyai-tts-1`.\n- `base_url`: the US data zone by default; `wss://tts.eu.assemblyai.com` keeps data in the EU.\n- `word_timestamps`: per-word timings (default `True`). With\n  `AgentSession(use_tts_aligned_transcript=True)`, LiveKit uses them to sync the transcript and to\n  record an interrupted reply up to the word the user heard.\n\nCall `tts.prewarm()` to open the session before the first reply.\n", "description_content_type": "text/markdown", "docs_url": null, "download_url": null, "downloads": {"last_day": -1, "last_month": -1, "last_week": -1}, "dynamic": null, "home_page": null, "keywords": "ai, audio, livekit, realtime, video, voice, webrtc", "license": null, "license_expression": "Apache-2.0", "license_files": null, "maintainer": null, "maintainer_email": null, "name": "livekit-plugins-assemblyai", "package_url": "https://pypi.org/project/livekit-plugins-assemblyai/", "platform": null, "project_url": "https://pypi.org/project/livekit-plugins-assemblyai/", "project_urls": {"Documentation": "https://docs.livekit.io", "Source": "https://github.com/livekit/agents", "Website": "https://livekit.io/"}, "provides_extra": null, "release_url": "https://pypi.org/project/livekit-plugins-assemblyai/1.8.13/", "requires_dist": ["livekit-agents>=1.8.13"], "requires_python": ">=3.10.0", "summary": "Agent Framework plugin for AssemblyAI", "version": "1.8.13", "yanked": false, "yanked_reason": null}, "release_dates": {"0.1.0": "2024-11-27T21:27:33.862624Z", "0.2.1": "2024-12-04T17:12:52.789375Z", "0.2.2": "2024-12-31T05:17:22.124781Z", "0.2.3": "2025-03-06T17:21:08.106391Z", "0.2.4": "2025-05-19T16:57:26.832577Z", "1.0.0": "2025-04-10T09:04:49.364637Z", "1.0.0.dev4": "2025-03-19T19:17:54.997630Z", "1.0.0.dev5": "2025-03-19T19:25:48.994350Z", "1.0.0rc1": "2025-03-26T21:38:22.008392Z", "1.0.0rc2": "2025-03-27T01:03:15.729964Z", "1.0.0rc3": "2025-03-27T01:27:00.787185Z", "1.0.0rc4": "2025-03-29T17:45:56.023264Z", "1.0.0rc5": "2025-04-03T00:35:56.786190Z", "1.0.0rc6": "2025-04-03T19:00:57.079269Z", "1.0.0rc7": "2025-04-07T15:04:52.037556Z", "1.0.0rc8": "2025-04-07T15:20:07.229018Z", "1.0.0rc9": "2025-04-07T22:45:30.615753Z", "1.0.1": "2025-04-10T09:10:46.038659Z", "1.0.10": "2025-04-10T09:18:18.071477Z", "1.0.11": "2025-04-10T09:23:45.198600Z", "1.0.12": "2025-04-15T10:32:08.487922Z", "1.0.13": "2025-04-15T18:20:23.814218Z", "1.0.14": "2025-04-22T15:32:37.232195Z", "1.0.15": "2025-04-22T15:42:56.865367Z", "1.0.16": "2025-04-22T19:38:44.529775Z", "1.0.17": "2025-04-24T19:52:48.367484Z", "1.0.18": "2025-05-01T08:37:00.623333Z", "1.0.19": "2025-05-03T22:39:09.113058Z", "1.0.2": "2025-04-10T09:13:10.315757Z", "1.0.20": "2025-05-08T15:32:45.744895Z", "1.0.21": "2025-05-15T01:24:33.106716Z", "1.0.22": "2025-05-17T13:11:20.184074Z", "1.0.23": "2025-05-29T20:15:53.755273Z", "1.1.0": "2025-06-10T11:15:50.032782Z", "1.1.1": "2025-06-10T16:03:22.001328Z", "1.1.2": "2025-06-20T14:21:48.578204Z", "1.1.3": "2025-06-21T00:33:27.385682Z", "1.1.4": "2025-06-25T13:23:56.914397Z", "1.1.5": "2025-06-30T16:22:12.342744Z", "1.1.6": "2025-07-10T17:32:11.373885Z", "1.1.7": "2025-07-15T21:21:20.647142Z", "1.2.0": "2025-07-17T18:35:56.344736Z", "1.2.1": "2025-07-17T18:41:08.318252Z", "1.2.10": "2025-09-18T19:13:05.796443Z", "1.2.11": "2025-09-18T19:14:48.121826Z", "1.2.12": "2025-09-29T04:48:37.848188Z", "1.2